<title>USA: Centigram Communications names chairman.</title>
<headline>Centigram Communications names chairman.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Calif. 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Centigram Communications Corp said on Tuesday it had named Dean Morton, a director and former chief operating officer of Hewlett-Packard Co, as chairman.</p>
<p>Director Michael Jarvis was named a vice-chairman, the company said. It also said it had formed an operating committee to manage the company's daily operations while Centigram looked for a new chief executive officer.  </p>
<p>The company was continuing its search for a new CEO following the resignation of George Sollman on April 2, it said.</p>
<p>Sollman was named a vice-chairman of the board and would remain in this position until the end of the fiscal year, the company said.</p>
<p>Centigram was not immediately available to comment on whom Morton replaced as chairman.</p>
</text>
